first run
deploy.example.com did not accept your key SHA256:SAMPLE0000000000000000000000000000000000000
(~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub). The box says no more to a key it does not accept, so it is one of these:
no person or signer line on the box lists it; your address is outside the from list on every grant
you hold; deploy.example.com is not the box's main name; or the box's moteld is too old to take a
key's token at all. Send the operator the line `motel key` prints.

your key    SHA256:SAMPLE0000000000000000000000000000000000000
            ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub (the default file)

To be added, send the operator this line (motel key prints it too):
  person <name> ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMuTYJV40qpZ7rH7T4/BJP6ERoj5JgqFQwHIEBTe5wrn
  (one line when sent; P quits and prints it whole below your prompt)

r  try again (once; each refusal counts against the box's budget)     q  quit













